Package: infereportR
Type: Package
Title: Tables, Text and Figures for Statistical Results
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: person("R.", "Heller", , "raban.heller@uni-ulm.de",
    role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-8006-9742"))
Description: Formats finalized statistical results as tables, text and
    figures. Results follow the common result contract of 'infercalcR';
    stored estimates, intervals, p-values and method metadata are reported
    at full precision and are never recomputed. Its figure layer extends
    'ggplot2' with a black-and-white theme for papers, following the
    figure rules of the Publication Manual, 7th edition, of the American
    Psychological Association (2020, ISBN:978-1-4338-3216-1), and for
    slides; with scales that replace color with line types, point shapes
    and hatch patterns; and with direct labels and size presets.
    Inference layers run explicitly named 'infercalcR' procedures, label
    them with the package's own display strings and keep the full results
    retrievable from the figure; annotation layers draw precomputed results
    at explicit positions. A character mode redraws plots on a monospaced
    text grid in the style of 1980s home computers.
